Spinach And Cheese Stuffed Chicken Breasts
Chicken, Dinner, Gluten Free, SCD Recipes

Spinach And Cheese Stuffed Chicken Breasts

ComfyTummy 13 years ago No Comments
  • Facebook
Prev Article Next Article

I was in the mood for something a little different so I wanted to give these a try. If you’re not strictly on the Specific Carbohydrate Diet, these are yummy with Feta cheese. If you’re on the SCD, then it’s really easy to replace the Feta with Farmer’s Cheese instead. Farmer’s cheese is a bit less sharp, but equally flavorful.

Spinach And Cheese Stuffed Chicken Breasts
Ingredients
2 chicken breasts (sliced in half to make 4 cutlets)
1 tsp minced garlic or 1/2 tsp granulated garlic
1 tablespoon butter or coconut oil
1 (16 ounce) bag spinach (frozen works great)
1 cup Farmer’s Cheese (or feta if not on SCD)
paprika

Preheat oven to 350 F. Prepare chicken for stuffing by slicing the breasts in half horizontally and then pounding flat between two pieces of waxed paper. In a skillet over medium heat, saute spinach in butter and garlic until wilted and/or heated through. Add cheese and mix well. Distribute spinach mixture onto each chicken breast. Wrap chicken around mixture like you would a burrito and secure with a toothpick or tuck the loose side under as you place the stuffed chicken breast into a buttered baking dish. Sprinkle with paprika for a little extra color. Bake for 30 minutes. Serve.

Any extra spinach/cheese mixture makes a great side dish.

