ComfyTummy
More from this Author

I was diagnosed with severe Ulcerative Colitis in 2004 and erroneously told by a gastroenterologist that I would spend the rest of my life on prescription meds. I began researching and studying natural alternative treatments and discovered the Specific Carbohydrate Diet (SCD). Within a year, I was off all meds and had brought my body and digestive system back into balance and a state of health and healing. This blog documents my journey of health and healing through nature and nutrition. Please note: It is just that - a journey. Since there is so much misinformation, disinformation, and conflicting information on the internet and in this world about what is healthy, what is the best natural route to health, what works, what doesn't work, etc., most of what we find ourselves doing is trial and error to see what works for us because every one of us in unique and different and as such has different nutritional and physical needs, weaknesses, and conditions. What worked for me may not work for you. Information that I wrote about on this blog several years ago may no longer be true for me. As mentioned above, health, much like life, is a journey. Where I was two years ago is most likely not where I am today. However, it may be where you are and the information might be helpful to you on your journey. It may bring you one step closer to healing. What I know for sure is that Ulcerative Colitis is not an auto-immune disease. It can be cured, your body can heal from it, and it is not a life sentence of meds, surgeries, and illness.

